{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And their drink-offerings, half the hin.</b> Six logs, for the hin is twelve logs. <b>for the bull</b> — corresponding to Abraham: at six hours of the day, in the heat of the day, the angels came to him and he ran to the cattle. <b>And a third of the hin</b> — that is four logs — <b>for the ram</b> — corresponding to Isaac, who was offered up at four hours of the day. <b>And a quarter of the hin</b> — that is three logs, eighteen eggs — <b>for the lamb</b> — corresponding to Jacob, who prayed eighteen blessings, as it is said (Genesis 28:11): ״ויפגע במקום״, and פגיעה is nothing but prayer, as it is written (Jeremiah 7:16): ״ואל תפגע בי״." "<b>And you should be roused to ask</b> that we do not find in all the Torah the measurement of a quarter of the hin for a bull or a ram, but only for the lamb alone; and there is a secret in this matter, and in the verse (Leviticus 26:42): ״וזכרתי את בריתי יעקוב״ I have alluded to it." "<b>This is the burnt-offering of each new moon in its month.</b> That if its day passed, its offering was cancelled and there is no longer any make-up for it."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:45.927658607Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}